Corrected message:

Stop moves without a selection from clipping later paint strokes

With nothing selected, Move Selection and Move Selected Pixels fell
back to the canvas-sized placeholder selection, then marked it visible
and kept its shifted geometry after the drag. That left a real
selection that clipped every later paint tool to wherever the drag
ended. Both tools now leave the selection untouched when none was
active; Move Selection with no selection is a no-op and adds no undo
step.

Also fix moved or pasted content erasing art beneath it: finishing a
move or paste replaced the destination pixels outright (Source), so
transparent parts of the moved content punched holes in the layer.
It now composites with Over.

Adds regression tests for both.
